{"id":"41dde5973b6476f2182b288d9ce2826cde6ebd09","axis":"silent","repo":"microsoft/vscode","sha":"41dde5973b6476f2182b288d9ce2826cde6ebd09","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"src/vs/sessions/DESKTOP.md","lines":["@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@ Let **E** = editor content visible, **D** = detail panel visible. The pane suppo"," "," Only **Existing Sessions** share a persisted Editor/Details visibility profile. A New Session does not apply or capture that profile; on entry it hides Editor once only when the restored editor set contains no input other than the managed Changes and Empty Files inputs. Submit seeds the Existing profile. Automatically opening or focusing a session or chat never reveals a fully closed side pane; saved composition is applied only while the side pane is already visible. Explicit actions such as **Toggle Side Panel**, **Show Editor**, opening a file, or the session-header **Changes** pill may reveal it. The active editor selects the detail content: every diff editor selects Changes, while Empty Files and resources inside the active session workspace select Files."," ","+While the Changes editor is visible, an empty selected changeset hides the docked Changes detail only when it also has no CI checks, so useful checks and Reveal Checks remain available independently of the selected changeset. Loading preserves the last settled file-change availability. Content returning restores automatically hidden detail, but does not override an explicit user hide or reveal a closed side pane. This presentation-only hide preserves intended visibility across draft submission and does not change saved visibility preferences; an incoming owner's saved composition replaces the outgoing transient hide, and a Details-only pane remains available.","+"," In `chat`, workspace-backed draft and created chats remember their own composition while using the same session lifecycle and interaction policies. Saved owner state wins when the side pane is visible; focusing an owner while it is fully closed preserves the saved state without revealing it. An unsaved created chat uses the applicable Existing Session visibility defaults, and an unsaved draft follows the existing draft entry rules. An unvisited peer has no copied ordinary editors; its initial bottom visibility comes from the workbench rather than being forced hidden. **Toggle Side Panel** reopens the focused chat's own last-open Editor/Details combination. In `chat-shared`, existing workspace chats instead use one shared current/last-open composition and bottom visibility; a first-visit peer has empty ordinary editors without hiding those shared panes. Draft and Quick Chat visibility remains separate. Whole-pane close retains editors; Details-only collapse retains its existing restorable-editor and close-veto behavior. Collapsed editors, Files dismissal, and pending detail/tab intents remain per-chat in both modes."," "," **Size distribution when opening the side pane.** Opening the side pane from *closed* (e.g. clicking **Changes** while the chat is full-width) reveals the editor with `Sizing.Distribute`. The grid uses the revealed view's location to distribute its containing split. The Sessions part and side pane therefore receive equal space without either part computing a width. After that, side-pane sizes are **workbench-level, not per session**: the editor grid node width is owned by the workbench grid and persisted globally (`workbench.sessions.partSizes`), so once the user resizes the side pane it keeps that width — including across **session switches** (switching sessions does not change the side-pane width) and across reloads."],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/vs/sessions/LAYOUT_CONTROLLER.md","lines":["@@ -69,9 +69,9 @@ The side pane combines Editor content and the docked Auxiliary Bar detail. Its v"," "," `DesktopExistingSessionStrategy` owns the legacy Existing Session visibility profile and experimental created-chat composition. `DesktopDraftSessionStrategy` owns workspace-backed and workspace-less draft behavior and experimental draft composition. Quick Chat behavior is selected by the desktop controller and continues to map editor-bearing Quick Chats onto the shared Existing Session profile."," ","-`DesktopDockedTabsCoordinator` owns the managed Changes and Files tabs. `DesktopDetailPanelCoordinator` maps the active editor to Changes or Files detail content and publishes the related context keys. The strategies decide visibility before publishing a content target.","+`DesktopDockedTabsCoordinator` owns the managed Changes and Files tabs. `DesktopDetailPanelCoordinator` maps the active editor to Changes or Files detail content, publishes the related context keys, and retains transient hide state across the draft-to-created lifecycle transition. The strategies decide visibility before publishing a content target and clear outgoing transient state when applying an incoming saved composition."," ","-The Auxiliary Bar is visible only when it has an active view container. Browser and unsupported editor tabs may hide Details transiently; activating a supported Changes or file editor reveals the matching detail once while preserving later explicit user hides.","+The Auxiliary Bar is visible only when it has an active view container. Browser, unsupported editor tabs, and a visible Changes editor with neither selected file changes nor CI checks may hide Details transiently; activating a supported Changes or file editor reveals the matching detail when available while preserving later explicit user hides."," "," Closing the whole side pane keeps ordinary editors available for restoration. Entering Details-only closes non-docked tabs and captures restorable editors for reopening when Editor content is shown again. Registered live editors remain in the hidden editor group instead of being disposed, preserving runtime state that cannot be reconstructed."," "],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/vs/sessions/browser/parts/sessionsEmptyStateLayout.ts","lines":["@@ -52,6 +52,10 @@ export class SessionsEmptyStateLayout extends Disposable {"," \t\t}"," \t\tconst available = this.container.getBoundingClientRect();"," \t\tconst reference = this.reference.getBoundingClientRect();","+\t\t// Editors can render before the containing grid has committed its dimensions.","+\t\tif (available.height === 0 || reference.height === 0) {","+\t\t\treturn;","+\t\t}"," \t\tlet availableTop = available.top;"," \t\tfor (let sibling = this.elements[0].previousElementSibling; sibling; sibling = sibling.previousElementSibling) {"," \t\t\tconst bounds = sibling.getBoundingClientRect();"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/vs/sessions/common/sessionConfig.ts","lines":["@@ -9,8 +9,6 @@ export const USE_WORKTREE_SETTING = 'sessions.useWorktree';"," "," export const SESSIONS_CHAT_TABS_SETTING = 'sessions.showChatTabs';"," ","-export const SESSIONS_EMPTY_FILE_EDITOR_ACTIONS_SETTING = 'sessions.experimental.emptyFileEditorActions';","-"," /** Whether the Session Activity Bar is shown beside the active chat in the desktop Agents window. */"," export const SESSION_ACTIVITY_BAR_SETTING = 'sessions.showSessionActivityBar';"," "],"additions":0,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/vs/sessions/contrib/changes/browser/changesEmptyState.ts","lines":["@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@ import { NEW_FILE_TAB_COMMAND_ID } from '../../../common/sessionCommands.js';"," import { EmptyFileEditorInput } from '../../editor/browser/emptyFileEditorInput.js';"," "," export class ChangesEmptyState extends Disposable {","+\tprivate readonly emptyStateLayout: SessionsEmptyStateLayout;","+"," \tconstructor("," \t\tcontainer: HTMLElement,"," \t\t@IInstantiationService instantiationService: IInstantiationService,","@@ -29,7 +31,11 @@ export class ChangesEmptyState extends Disposable {"," \t\t\tariaLabel: localize('changes.emptyActions', \"Changes actions\"),"," \t\t\ttelemetrySource: 'changes.emptyState',"," \t